# PLACEHOLDER art for hemp_canvas. Warlon Mhite intends to redraw this.
#
# A folded bolt of cloth rather than a flat swatch: vanilla's cloth-ish items (leather, paper,
# phantom membrane) all read as a *thing with edges*, and a flat square of noise at 16x16 reads as a
# missing texture rather than as fabric. Both ends taper so the silhouette is not a rectangle —
# the texture linter flags near-perfect rectangles as placeholder-looking, and it is right to.
#
# The weave is faked with a two-tone checker whose tones sit close together, so it reads as texture
# rather than as stripes, with a bright lit fold at the top and a deep shadow pooling at the bottom
# to carry the contrast vanilla items average.

@palette canvas
. = none
# outline, a desaturated brown-green so it reads as undyed hemp and not as leather. Two tones,
# because the linter checks the *outline itself* for lighting direction: O is the lit upper-left
# edge, o the shaded lower-right one.
O = 5A5638
o = 262417
# the two weave tones
a = 9B9464
b = 8D8659
# lit top fold and the lit left edge — items are lit from the top left, so the highlight lives on
# the top and left and the shadow on the bottom and right. Getting this backwards is the single
# thing the texture linter catches most often, and it makes an item look inside-out at a glance.
h = D6CB90
# shadow where the bolt tapers away underneath
s = 4A472F
# the shaded right edge
r = 5D5940

@texture item/hemp_canvas 16x16 type=item palette=canvas
